- name: park
  id: kyttar_cordic_rotate
  parameters:
    affinity: ''
    alias: ''
    comment: 'ON CHIP: the FORWARD Park rotation, sign = -1 (rotate by -theta). Takes the measured stationary-frame
      current vector into the rotor frame, where the torque- and flux-producing components separate. A
      THREE-arm rendezvous: x, y and theta must land on three distinct faces.'
    device_id: '"kyttar_0"'
    sign: '-1'
    maxoutbuf: '0'
    minoutbuf: '0'
  states:
    bus_sink: false
    bus_source: false
    bus_structure: null
    coordinate:
    - 1308
    - 1135
    rotation: 0
    state: enabled
- name: sink_idq
  id: kyttar_sink
  parameters:
    affinity: ''
    alias: ''
    comment: "drains the measurement half's result: the rotor-frame currents (i_d, i_q) interleaved. Q15\
      \ floats \u2014 the sink emits word/32768."
    maxoutbuf: '0'
    minoutbuf: '0'
    device_id: '"kyttar_0"'
    hold_secs: '8.0'
    in_type: complex
    num_channels: '1'
    port_name: '"x16_out"'
    server_port: '58950'
    server_repeat: 'True'
    stream_id: '"ia"'
  states:
    bus_sink: false
    bus_source: false
    bus_structure: null
    coordinate:
    - 1568
    - 1097
    rotation: 0
    state: enabled
- name: idq_split
  id: blocks_deinterleave
  parameters:
    affinity: ''
    alias: ''
    blocksize: '1'
    comment: "split the recovered interleaved [i_d, i_q, i_d, i_q, ...] float stream into the two rails\
      \ the error former subtracts from. The kyttar sink emits FLOAT even for a complex on-chip stream\
      \ \u2014 the rails come back interleaved."
    maxoutbuf: '0'
    minoutbuf: '0'
    num_streams: '2'
    type: float
    vlen: '1'
  states:
    bus_sink: false
    bus_source: false
    bus_structure: null
    coordinate:
    - 1828
    - 1127
    rotation: 0
    state: enabled
